course: dictionary
lesson: 4145
title: Glove: one word, many jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. Glove is a good example. Its main meaning is a covering for your hand, with a separate place for each finger and the thumb.
explain: The words around a glove tell you which job it does. «Sparklers are held with gloves at arm's length» shows the gloves keep your hands safe. A baseball glove is a different kind of glove, used in a sport.
explain: Ask yourself: what would this glove be for? Then check your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A glove is a covering for your hand, with a separate place for each finger and the thumb.
fact: A mitten has no finger spaces. All your fingers share one part.
fact: «A pair of gloves» means two gloves, one for each hand.
fact: Gloves can keep your hands warm, clean or safe, for example from chemicals and germs.
fact: «Fit like a glove» means fit very well.
exercise: «Sparklers are held with gloves at arm's length and put into a bucket of water when they finish.» What are the gloves for? | To hold the bucket of water | To keep the sparklers dry in a box | *To protect the hands | To make the sparklers light faster
exercise: Which kind of glove is used in a sport? | A winter glove | A mitten with no finger spaces | A rubber glove for washing up | *A baseball glove
exercise: How many gloves make one pair? | Five | *Two | One | Ten
test: «In hospitals, sealed plastic syringes, gloves and tubes keep medicine and tools free of germs.» What do the gloves do here? | Make the hospital warmer | Show the nurse's name | Hold the medicine tight | *Help keep things free of germs
test: What is the difference between a glove and a mitten? | A glove is only for sport, and a mitten is only for hospitals | *A mitten has no separate finger spaces, but a glove has one for each finger and the thumb | There is no difference at all | A glove has no finger spaces, but a mitten does
exam: In «white kid gloves», what is a kid glove? | A glove with no fingers | A glove for a child | *A soft glove made of young goat's leather | A glove used in a sport
